1908-02-15||AS:1||South Australian supplementary Senate poll: Joseph Vardon won. Restored the party of the original 1906 winner after that return and James O'Loghlin's intervening Labor appointment were voided. Not a normal casual-vacancy appointment. Full chamber on this date not independently verified.
